  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical capacitors <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></math> charged to the same potential <math><mn>5</mn><mi>V</mi></math> are connected in two different circuits as shown below at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the charge on capacitors <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> at time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is <math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub></math> respectively, then (Here <math><mi>e</mi></math> is the base of natural logarithm)<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/87177991-a74d-479d-8bcb-e0ca05b76539-image.png\" style=\"width: 390px; height: 170px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "aZrs7",
      "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
